-- title:
--   Birkhoff's near family: continuity of the first crossing
-- statement:
--   Fix $0<\mu<1$ and a Jacobi energy $-c$ below the first critical value. Let $\Sigma_{\mu,c}$ be the selected Levi-Civita component and $\varphi$ a continuous flow on it generated by the Hamiltonian vector field of $K_{\mu,c}$. Let $N(r)$ and $F(r)$ be the perpendicular near and far starts, and $(\sigma,\eta)$ the shooting coordinates (velocity sine and depth). For a near arc of length $\tau$ the crossing state is $\varphi_{-\tau}s$; for a far arc it is $\varphi_\tau s$.
--
--   **Continuity of the first crossing (near family).** Suppose $r_0>0$ and the state $s_0=N(r_0)$ lies on $\Sigma_{\mu,c}$ and admits a near shooting arc of length $\tau_0$. Then for every $\varepsilon>0$ there is $\delta>0$ with the following property. For every $r$ with $|r-r_0|<\delta$, the state $N(r)$ lies on $\Sigma_{\mu,c}$ and admits a near shooting arc of some length $\tau$ whose crossing coordinates satisfy
--   $$
--   \operatorname{dist}\bigl((\sigma,\eta)(\text{crossing of }N(r)),\,(\sigma,\eta)(\text{crossing of }s_0)\bigr)<\varepsilon .
--   $$
--
--   In words, the set of good parameters is open, and on it the crossing coordinates depend continuously on the start. This is the transversality step of Birkhoff's shooting argument: the arc leaves the axis transversally, crosses the vertical line transversally, and stays a positive distance from the boundary of the admissible region in between.
-- source:
--   Liu--Salomao, Finite energy foliations in the restricted three-body problem, https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.17867v2, Section 5, proof of Theorem 5.1 (pp. 30-31): the curves Gamma_1, Gamma_2, their continuity and endpoints; after G. D. Birkhoff, The restricted problem of three bodies, Rend. Circ. Mat. Palermo 39 (1915), Sections 16-18 (Collected Mathematical Papers Vol. 1, pp. 731-741).

import Definitions.Def_BirkhoffShootingArcs

namespace BirkhoffGlobalSection

theorem birkhoff_near_arc_continuity (μ c : ℝ)
    (hμ0 : 0 < μ) (hμ1 : μ < 1)
    (hc : belowFirstCriticalValue μ c)
    (φ : Flow ℝ (LeftEnergyState μ c))
    (hφ : IsLeviCivitaHamiltonianFlow μ c φ)
    (r₀ : ℝ) (hr₀ : 0 < r₀) (x₀ : LeftEnergyState μ c) (τ₀ : ℝ)
    (hx₀ : (x₀ : Phase) = nearShootingStart μ c r₀) (harc : IsNearShootingArc φ x₀ τ₀) :
    ∀ ε > 0, ∃ δ > 0, ∀ r : ℝ, |r - r₀| < δ →
      ∃ x : LeftEnergyState μ c, (x : Phase) = nearShootingStart μ c r ∧ ∃ τ : ℝ, IsNearShootingArc φ x τ ∧
        dist (shootingCoordinates μ ((φ (-τ) x : LeftEnergyState μ c) : Phase))
          (shootingCoordinates μ ((φ (-τ₀) x₀ : LeftEnergyState μ c) : Phase)) < ε := by sorry

end BirkhoffGlobalSection
